# What the PRODUCTION server keeps: never in the package, never deleted there.
#
# One path per line, from the project root; * matches within a folder. The
# upload mirrors the package with --delete, so anything not listed here that
# the package does not carry is removed from the server.
#
# runtime.local.php and .well-known/ are always kept, listed or not.
#
# Development tooling never reaches production, and needs no listing:
# deploy-prod.yml leaves out the probe directory, runtime.dev.php, the
# deployment metadata, LLM.txt, tests/ and the repository's own material —
# the agent folders, every Markdown file, docs/, captures/ —
# fails the build if any of it is in the package, and removes it from the
# server if it is found there. The production smoke check then asserts the
# probe URLs return 404.
#
# See policies/production.md.

# This server's own settings (never uploaded; the server's copy stays)
runtime.local.php
runtime.local.example.php

# Runtime state the application owns on the server
cache
logs
data
